     "uri_web/synthesize.py:341",
     "uri_a2ui/validate.py:150"
    ],
    "id": "R39-01",
    "owner_decision": false,
    "severity": "HIGH",
    "suggested_fix": "Do not special-case one spacing pattern. Fold look-alikes per character (0->o, 1/I/|->l or i, Unicode skeleton) over the whole normalised text before running the same spaced-ending detection that already catches 'go v', 'c  o  m', '(c o m)' and tabs, so the digit and letter forms are handled by one path; and extend the mask span to cover the whole folded ending. Add regression tests for the forms above.",
    "title": "R38-01 repair incomplete (R1-01/R31-01 class): _SPELT_SINGLES reads only single characters separated by single plain spaces, so partially spelt or differently spaced endings with an ASCII look-alike digit ('g0 v', 'g 0v', '0r g', '0 rg', 'c  0  m', '(c 0 m)', 'c\\t0\\tm', 'i  0') are not links, although the letter forms ('go v', 'g ov', 'or g', 'c  o  m', '(c o m)', 'c\\to\\tm', 'i  o') are; they pass has_link_or_contact, mask_links, verify(), extractive(), the research surface and the A2UI validator (W1-AC12/AC15, D16/D29)"
